  "notes": "Composition mapped to BiGG (mapper + salt dissociation); presence-based bounds; paper_amount retained. Added via GrowthDB curation.",
  "verification": "paper-verified (corrected via workflow)",
  "verification_evidence": "Whole-cell Michaelis-Menten kinetics were measured ... Cultures were grown in medium with 1 mM acetate and 2 mM NO3− and a H2/CO2/N2 (5:5:90) headspace. After NO3−/ NO2− depletion, bottles underwent three vacuum-pressurization cycles with N2 gas, followed by the addition of 10 mM NO2− and H2 (100-100 000 ppmv) ... [base medium] contained, per liter of deionized water: 4.76 mmol NaCl, 0.47 mmol CaC",
  "verification_confidence": "high",
